WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:29.660
[Music]

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.240
[Narrator:] Yes, the story of tuberculosis
is a dramatic one.

00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:43.180
 Tuberculosis is older than history.

00:00:43.456 --> 00:00:45.980
It's never given civilized men peace.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:53.169
No one, artist or statesman, rich or poor,
young or old, is immune. Once it was a hopeless case,

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:59.249
but now, thanks to our knowledge, it can
be brought under control.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.059
Now let me tell you about it. 

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:13.100
Tuberculosis is caused by a germ so small, thousands could pass through a pinhole without crowding.

00:01:13.282 --> 00:01:16.342
We know exactly what it looks like.

00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:22.459
The tubercle bacillus is a living plant. It
grows and reproduces. 

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:28.780
It dies quickly in boiling water or sunshine, but thrives in the human body.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.480
How does the germ get into the body?

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:36.900
Well, careless people who have the disease may spit on the floor or sidewalk. 

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.060
Mixed with the dust, the germs may be blown about and breathed by others.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.960
This child, for example, may carry the germs on the lollipop to her mouth,

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.140
or germs may be left on any article that touches the lips.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:56.969
The next person who puts one of these articles into his mouth gives the germs a chance

00:01:56.969 --> 00:02:02.329
to get into his body, but far more important
is the danger of direct contact,

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:08.100
especially lip contact of one who has the disease with one who hasn't.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:13.710
How can our little friend, John, for example, escape getting into his lungs some of the

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.440
tuberculosis germs of his Aunt Alice, who
has been visiting.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:24.340
She loves him dearly, but doesn't seem to
realize that what she calls her chronic bronchitis

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:26.730
is really tuberculosis.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:31.250
Now let us suppose that some of the germs of Aunt Alice's lungs 

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.440
have actually made their way into John's lungs.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:40.000
They've gained a foothold here in the lung substance. What happens then?

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.470
We have focused a powerful microscope on the spot 

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:50.730
and here we see the germs attached to the lung substance. John is now infected.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:54.760
Soon the germs increase in number and begin to spread.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:59.760
But see?  The cells of the body seem to be waking up. 

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:03.860
They are jailing them in a tight little capsule called a tubercle.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:13.220
It's a battle royale now, but this time the body wins. Lucky John.

00:03:13.939 --> 00:03:18.459
Of course, these are just diagrams, but that is about what happens.             

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.760
There you see the first tubercule.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:26.879
Eventually a gritty substance called calcium takes the place of the destroyed lung substance,

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.240
and the little shell becomes hard and stony.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:36.640
In fact, it is this gritty material that casts
its shadow on the x-ray film.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.600
Here is an x-ray picture of such a first tubercle. 

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:45.560
The disease in this case gets no further than that first tubercle,

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.940
except that some germs may escape to the nearby lymph glands or nodes.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:56.720
Lymph glands serve as filters, stopping germs from spreading over the body.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:03.220
Here they are stopped. The lymph glands may suffer some damage, but this is repaired,

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:08.409
just as in the lung substance. These two show on the x-ray film.

00:04:08.409 --> 00:04:11.840
No two cases of tuberculosis are exactly alike,              

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.040
but what we have seen probably happens very commonly.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:21.100
Many, many persons who are infected as children will never know it and are none the worse for it.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.460
But on with the story.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:30.968
John has grown. He's a senior in high school now and he's been infected again, though he doesn't know it.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:35.150
Perhaps his aunt has come
to live with the family.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:40.470
Because John had already been infected, the cells of his body have been stimulated or

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:45.090
sensitized to further attacks of these
tuberculosis germs.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:51.510
Now, in their eagerness to surround the germs and protect the body from them, the cells

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:58.740
often destroy themselves, thus giving the
germs a chance to spread, and once they get started,

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:04.160
the germs soon destroy tissue and
do real damage until they are checked.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:09.820
Besides, John was a bit careless. He used up too much of his energy. 

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.680
Hard work at school, strenuous athletics, out late at night.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:20.720
Let's look again at John's lungs. Yes, the
original tubercle is still there,

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:29.060
firm and hard, and the healed lymph nodes. But look, there's a bit of trouble here.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:35.890
Nothing to get excited about, you say. Yet
that is the real beginning of serious tuberculosis.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:40.340
John has no symptoms. He probably feels perfectly well.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:46.840
He wouldn't think of going to a doctor. A
dark tragedy is staring John in the face, 

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:53.100
but lucky John, the enemy was discovered. How?

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:58.840
In the up-to-date high school he attended,
the tuberculin test was offered to all students.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:06.030
This test is simple and harmless. Well, here is John at the head of the line.            

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:10.440
A few drops of a liquid called tuberculin is injected into the skin.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:17.440
Hurt? Well, yes, about like a mosquito bite
and a lot less harmful than many a mosquito bite.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:21.060
Two days later the test is read. 

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:25.210
If the spot is raised and reddened, it is called positive.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:31.540
What does that mean? Only that at some time, tuberculosis germs have entered the body.                                

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:35.510
In this school, 30 percent of the children were positive. 

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:41.700
So these were x-rayed to see if the germs were doing any damage. John was one of them.                            

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:46.400
No need to x-ray the others because, without infection there can be no tuberculosis.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:52.630
When John's family doctor looked at the developed film, this is what he saw.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:07:00.220
The old shadow scarcely visible and here in the upper part of the right lung, some suspicious shadows.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.240
Not very serious.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:06.140
John spent a short time in bed and then he
went back to school, 

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:11.800
but what bothered the doctor was, where did John get his infection and his re-infection?

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:17.480
He knew that every case comes from another, so naturally he sent for John's parents.

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:22.351
[Doctor:] I just wanted to make sure, Mrs.
Brown, that John did not get his infection at home.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:26.860
Your lungs are absolutely all right
and so are Mr. Brown's, 

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:30.480
and Jean shows only a positive tuberculin test.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:35.280
[Mrs. Brown:] Doctor, my sister, Alice, has
come to live with us again. She coughs a lot.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.430
[Doctor:] By all means ask her to come     
see me.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:44.580
[Narrator:] To make a long story short, the
doctor found that Aunt Alice had an old chronic tuberculosis.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.600
There were tubercle bacilli in her sputum.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:52.790
See this cavity in the lungs? From it comes
a steady stream of germs. 

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:57.920
Yet, she didn't feel sick enough to complain. There are many such people. 

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.947
For John's sake, she consented to go to the sanatorium.

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:15.480
Now suppose we pick up the story where we left it with John. Just a little inflammation here.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.740
With rest in bed, the little tubercles
which cast these shadows harden 

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.240
and quickly stop the spread of the disease.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:29.460
Suppose this had not been discovered. What then? Well, it probably would have spread.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:35.776
Watch this spot. It is being hollowed out. Now, it is a cavity.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:43.240
Inside, the germs are growing fast and many of them escape into the air passages and are coughed up.

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:49.120
A veritable factory of germs is
such a cavity; serious for the patient

00:08:49.129 --> 00:08:52.888
and dangerous to all those with whom he comes in close contact.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:09:00.680
It takes years of rest in bed to heal it. It
sometimes never heals but goes on to death,

00:09:01.279 --> 00:09:10.055
but I'm happy to say that even this serious condition is not hopeless today, when there's a way of collapsing a diseased lung.

00:09:10.055 --> 00:09:12.436
Let me show you how that is done.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:20.500
It requires a simple operation called pneumothorax, which means putting air into the chest.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:26.359
Since the lung is soft, it is easily collapsed, as one would squeeze a sponge.

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:32.949
The cavity is closed and that stops the manufacture of germs. 

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:37.140
It rests the lung and gives it                            
a chance to heal.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:44.060
The cough stops, the fever goes down and best of all no more germs are spit up.

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:48.380
That is exactly the way John's Aunt Alice was treated.

00:09:48.389 --> 00:09:54.600
Of course, the air gradually leaks out but
it is an easy matter to put in more air every

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.520
two weeks or so until the lung has healed completely. 

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:08.955
Then gradually the lung is allowed to re-expand. Pneumothorax is a lifesaver for thousands.

00:10:08.955 --> 00:10:13.220
I'm sure that you now appreciate that the
earlier tuberculosis is discovered, the more

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:18.557
the more certain is the cure. Delay is not only dangerous, it is costly.

00:10:18.725 --> 00:10:21.905
[Woman:] But, doctor, what is the answer to this problem? 

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:26.420
Surely once they get tuberculosis, the money is well spent on the cure?

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:31.627
[Narrator:] Yes, but money well spent in prevention will make cure unnecessary.

00:10:31.966 --> 00:10:38.110
We must beat our silent enemy to it and strike him down before he strikes us.

00:10:39.517 --> 00:10:46.970
Every young person from 15 to 25 years ought to have the benefit of the tuberculin test

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:57.760
and the x-ray, and someday I hope that we shall make a routine practice of testing every child

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.116
from babyhood with tuberculin.

00:11:00.412 --> 00:11:06.752
You spot the enemy at his first shadow. I
am confident you young people

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:12.107
will see the victorious end of this struggle.

